  "llm_raw_response": "<description>\n[\n  {\"task_type\": \"Drag & Drop Interface\", \"description\": \"Add a drag-and-drop task board to the About page where users can organize PostgreSQL feature priorities. The board should have three columns (Planned, In Progress, Completed) with draggable feature cards, visual drag handles, drop zone highlighting, ghost elements during drag, and persist the order to localStorage.\"}\n]\n</description>\n<search_replace path=\"about.html\">\n<search>\n<h2>Why use PostgreSQL?</h2>\n<p>\n  PostgreSQL comes with <a>many features</a> aimed to help developers build applications, administrators to protect data integrity and build fault-tolerant environments, and help you manage your data no matter how big or small the dataset.  In addition to being <a>free and open source</a>, PostgreSQL is highly extensible. For example, you can define your own data types, build out custom functions, even write code from <a>different programming languages</a> without recompiling your database!\n</p>\n<p>PostgreSQL tries to conform with the <a>SQL standard</a> where such conformance does not contradict traditional features or could lead to poor architectural decisions. Many of the features required by the SQL standard are supported, though sometimes with slightly differing syntax or function. Further moves towards conformance can be expected over time. As of the version 18 release in September 2025, PostgreSQL conforms to at least 170 of the 177 mandatory features for SQL:2023\n</search>\n<replace>\n<h2>Why use PostgreSQL?</h2>\n<p>\n  PostgreSQL comes with <a>many features</a> aimed to help developers build applications, administrators to protect data integrity and build fault-tolerant environments, and help you manage your data no matter how big or small the dataset.  In addition to being <a>free and open source</a>, PostgreSQL is highly extensible. For example, you can define your own data types, build out custom functions, even write code from <a>different programming languages</a> without recompiling your database!\n</p>\n<p>PostgreSQL tries to conform with the <a>SQL standard</a> where such conformance does not contradict traditional features or could lead to poor architectural decisions. Many of the features required by the SQL standard are supported, though sometimes with slightly differing syntax or function. Further moves towards conformance can be expected over time. As of the version 18 release in September 2025, PostgreSQL conforms to at least 170 of the 177 mandatory features for SQL:2023\n</p>\n\n<h2>Feature Priority Board</h2>\n<p>Drag and drop cards between columns to prioritize PostgreSQL features. Your layout is automatically saved.</p>\n<div id=\"feature-board\" class=\"feature-board\">\n  <div class=\"board-column\" data-status=\"planned\">\n    <h3 class=\"column-header\"><span class=\"drag-handle\">&#9776;</span> Planned</h3>\n    <div class=\"drop-zone\" data-status=\"planned\">\n      <div class=\"feature-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-id=\"1\">\n        <span class=\"card-handle\">&#9776;</span>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">Parallel Query Execution</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">Enhance parallel worker coordination for complex queries</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"feature-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-id=\"2\">\n        <span class=\"card-handle\">&#9776;</span>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">Logical Replication Improvements</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">Conflict resolution and automatic failover support</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"feature-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-id=\"3\">\n        <span class=\"card-handle\">&#9776;</span>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">JIT Compilation Enhancements</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">Expand LLVM JIT to more query plan nodes</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"board-column\" data-status=\"inprogress\">\n    <h3 class=\"column-header\"><span class=\"drag-handle\">&#9776;</span> In Progress</h3>\n    <div class=\"drop-zone\" data-status=\"inprogress\">\n      <div class=\"feature-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-id=\"4\">\n        <span class=\"card-handle\">&#9776;</span>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">Incremental Materialized Views</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">Refresh materialized views without full recomputation</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"feature-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-id=\"5\">\n        <span class=\"card-handle\">&#9776;</span>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">Table Access Method API</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">Pluggable storage engines for specialized workloads</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"board-column\" data-status=\"completed\">\n    <h3 class=\"column-header\"><span class=\"drag-handle\">&#9776;</span> Completed</h3>\n    <div class=\"drop-zone\" data-status=\"completed\">\n      <div class=\"feature-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-id=\"6\">\n        <span class=\"card-handle\">&#9776;</span>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">JSONB Performance Optimizations</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">Faster GIN index builds and query execution</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"feature-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-id=\"7\">\n        <span class=\"card-handle\">&#9776;</span>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">SCRAM-SHA-256 Authentication</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">Modern password authentication replacing MD5</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<style>\n.feature-board {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 20px;\n  margin: 20px 0 40px;\n  min-height: 400px;\n}\n.board-column {\n  flex: 1;\n  background: #f8f9fa;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 15px;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n.column-header {\n  font-size: 16px;\n  margin: 0 0 12px;\n  padding-bottom: 10px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #dee2e6;\n  color: #495057;\n}\n.drag-handle, .card-handle {\n  cursor: grab;\n  color: #adb5bd;\n  margin-right: 8px;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  user-select: none;\n}\n.card-handle {\n  float: right;\n  margin-right: 0;\n  margin-left: 8px;\n}\n.drop-zone {\n  flex: 1;\n  min-height: 100px;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  transition: background-color 0.2s ease;\n}\n.drop-zone.drag-over {\n  background-color: #e7f3ff;\n  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px #007bff;\n}\n.feature-card {\n  background: #fff;\n  border: 1px solid #dee2e6;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\n  cursor: grab;\n  transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;\n  position: relative;\n}\n.feature-card:hover {\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\n}\n.feature-card.dragging {\n  opacity: 0.5;\n  transform: rotate(2deg);\n}\n.feature-card .card-title {\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: #212529;\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\n  font-size: 14px;\n}\n.feature-card .card-desc {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: #6c757d;\n  line-height: 1.4;\n}\n.ghost-card {\n  background: #e9ecef;\n  border: 2px dashed #adb5bd;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n</style>\n\n<script>\n(function() {\n  const STORAGE_KEY = 'pg_feature_board_state';\n  let draggedEl = null;\n  let ghostEl = null;\n\n  function saveState() {\n    const state = {};\n    document.querySelectorAll('.drop-zone').forEach(zone => {\n      const status = zone.dataset.status;\n      const ids = Array.from(zone.querySelectorAll('.feature-card')).map(c => c.dataset.id);\n      state[status] = ids;\n    });\n    localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(state));\n  }\n\n  function loadState() {\n    try {\n      const saved = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);\n      if (!saved) return;\n      const state = JSON.parse(saved);\n      const allCards = new Map();\n      document.querySelectorAll('.feature-card').forEach(card => {\n        allCards.set(card.dataset.id, card);\n      });\n      Object.entries(state).forEach(([status, ids]) => {\n        const zone = document.querySelector(`.drop-zone[data-status=\"${status}\"]`);\n        if (!zone) return;\n        ids.forEach(id => {\n          const card = allCards.get(id);\n          if (card) zone.appendChild(card);\n        });\n      });\n    } catch (e) {\n      console.warn('Failed to load board state', e);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function createGhost() {\n    const ghost = document.createElement('div');\n    ghost.className = 'ghost-card';\n    ghost.style.height = draggedEl.offsetHeight + 'px';\n    return ghost;\n  }\n\n  function initDragAndDrop() {\n    document.querySelectorAll('.feature-card').forEach(card => {\n      card.addEventListener('dragstart', function(e) {\n        draggedEl = this;\n        this.classList.add('dragging');\n        e.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'move';\n        e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', this.dataset.id);\n        ghostEl = createGhost();\n        setTimeout(() => {\n          if (ghostEl && draggedEl) {\n            draggedEl.parentNode.insertBefore(ghostEl, draggedEl.nextSibling);\n          }\n        }, 0);\n      });\n\n      card.addEventListener('dragend', function() {\n        this.classList.remove('dragging');\n        if (ghostEl && ghostEl.parentNode) {\n          ghostEl.parentNode.removeChild(ghostEl);\n        }\n        ghostEl = null;\n        draggedEl = null;\n        document.querySelectorAll('.drop-zone').forEach(z => z.classList.remove('drag-over'));\n        saveState();\n      });\n    });\n\n    document.querySelectorAll('.drop-zone').forEach(zone => {\n      zone.addEventListener('dragover', function(e) {\n        e.preventDefault();\n        e.dataTransfer.dropEffect = 'move';\n        this.classList.add('drag-over');\n      });\n\n      zone.addEventListener('dragleave', function(e) {\n        this.classList.remove('drag-over');\n      });\n\n      zone.addEventListener('drop', function(e) {\n        e.preventDefault();\n        this.classList.remove('drag-over');\n        if (!draggedEl) return;\n        const afterElement = getDragAfterElement(this, e.clientY);\n        if (afterElement) {\n          this.insertBefore(draggedEl, afterElement);\n        } else {\n          this.appendChild(draggedEl);\n        }\n        if (ghostEl && ghostEl.parentNode) {\n          ghostEl.parentNode.removeChild(ghostEl);\n        }\n        ghostEl = null;\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  function getDragAfterElement(container, y) {\n    const draggableElements = [...container.querySelectorAll('.feature-card:not(.dragging)')];\n    return draggableElements.reduce((closest, child) => {\n      const box = child.getBoundingClientRect();\n      const offset = y - box.top - box.height / 2;\n      if (offset < 0 && offset > closest.offset) {\n        return { offset: offset, element: child };\n      } else {\n        return closest;\n      }\n    }, { offset: Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY }).element;\n  }\n\n  loadState();\n  initDragAndDrop();\n})();\n</script>\n</replace>\n</search_replace>",
